**Owner decision 2026-11-26: implementation and heavy acceptance have different owners.** Cursor implements the selected design, constructs specified deterministic proof tools, runs focused unit/contract tests, changed-file quality checks and proportionate cheap local integration checks, and commits a coherent implementation receipt. The design/planning ChatGPT and human owner own heavy acceptance: broad builds/suites, infrastructure lifecycle and fault/recovery runs, multi-service/browser/end-to-end exercises, release upgrades, long-running or costly probes and other substantial operational proof. ChatGPT selects exact commands, target, prerequisites, expected outcomes, timeouts, stop/cleanup and evidence; the human runs the bounded batch in their terminal and returns results for ChatGPT to interpret and record. Prefer one reproducible scripted batch over repeated paid-agent terminal orchestration. No heavy acceptance by Cursor unless the owner explicitly delegates that named proof; elapsed time alone is not a hard cutoff, and essential focused negative tests are not skipped to save tokens. The planner partitions the existing acceptance matrix by executor before commission (or at the next checkpoint of an in-flight Change). This changes who runs proof, not its required tier, safety, or integration gate.

When Cursor completes source work and its assigned cheap checks, it commits on the Change branch, reports exact SHA, owned paths, tests/results, known failures, remaining acceptance commands and resource/collision state, and stops at **IMPLEMENTED — ACCEPTANCE PENDING** (an open Change checkpoint, not a new lifecycle category or Done). Preserve the linked worktree and do not merge, archive or retire while mandatory heavy acceptance is pending. ChatGPT/owner take over proof without re-dispatching Cursor merely to run commands; fix ordinary source defects through a bounded implementation follow-up, and return architecture contradictions to the planner. Record acceptance against the exact tested SHA, then the named integration custodian reconciles current main, checks affected proof on any changed seams, integrates, reconciles documentation/evidence and retires clean work. Cursor may perform mechanical join/retirement after receiving the accepted proof receipt, or close cheap-only Changes autonomously when every required gate is met. No extra ceremonial approval or duplicate test sweep. This explicit responsibility split supersedes older unconditional whole-Change Cursor acceptance/closure language; never infer live mutation permission, waive essential gates, or claim unrun proof.

# Cursor execution: thin adapter

**Development resource courtesy:** Treat the active dev cluster as shared scarce compute. Change execution does not imply reserving or starting a stack. Follow [the dev runbook](../../docs/runbooks/dev-worktree-stacks.md): use cheap source-only tests when valid; do not speculatively start six pods; on partially healthy or capacity-failed startup, park **all your own attempted workloads** and confirm no own processes/ports remain, leaving every other agent, reservation and persistent tenant untouched. Never repeatedly retry without changed capacity. Demand-driven `dev:reserve` / profiles are planned DXK10 interfaces, not currently proven commands.

Read root [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md), the commissioned Change's `CHANGE.md`/`TASKS.md`, and the [canonical parent policy](../../.agents/references/bounded-parent-orchestration.md); **those own the rules**. Do not duplicate lifecycle/branch/batch policy here.

**Before first implementation edit:** on a dedicated `change/<id>-<slug>` branch based on the packet's real integration target, run `node scripts/repo-tools/change-branch-guard.mjs --change <ID> --target <reference-branch>`. If the target moved, reconcile it rather than resetting. A **separate linked worktree is mandatory per commissioned Change**, even if no other chat is active. Never switch the user's primary checkout. No worktree per T-ID. Run the branch guard inside the dedicated worktree.

**Dispatch fast path:** `do <Change ID>` means finish the already-selected Change, not perform an architecture review. After necessary branch/worktree/anchor checks, select the first ready T-ID and apply the [canonical one-time delegation decision](../../.agents/references/bounded-parent-orchestration.md#0a-budget-first-composer-dispatcher-contract-2026-11-21). **Default: launch one Composer Standard implementer for the first substantive PATCH task.** A tiny mechanical edit already in context may be done directly, but one-file security/state/test edits are not categorically tiny. Do not implement a succession of substantive T-IDs in the parent or deliberate repeatedly about model routing. Send children only their T-ID and concrete anchors; parent owns assigned cheap proof and source integration; archive, squash/push and safe retirement follow accepted proof, including ChatGPT/owner heavy acceptance when required. No unapproved next Change.

**Parent:** default Composer Standard; if the packet explicitly proves a safe independent wave, up to two disjoint children may run concurrently; otherwise one at a time. One commissioned Change proceeds through all its T-IDs and final join unless a genuine blocker occurs. Checkpoints are internal continuation points, **not instructions to stop and request owner approval**. Source/design missing from a supposedly Ready card returns to ChatGPT with the exact symbol or decision, not a paid Cursor investigation. The selected model in Cursor UI cannot be enforced by repository text; report any observed limitation accurately.

**Child:** assigned `DEPTH=VERIFY|PATCH|INVESTIGATE`, one T-ID, a few named source anchors, specific patch/normal/negative test and short receipt. No agent swarms, broad research, unrelated refactors, expensive-model self-upgrades, full suite per child, or shared-checkout commits. Verify only what the task needs. If a true architecture/permission/transaction contradiction appears, return file:symbol, failing assumption and reproducer to parent/ChatGPT. Ordinary unrelated local errors may be fixed with bounded diagnosis; do not loop on the same unexplained failure.

**Maintainability is part of implementation:** Follow [code craftsmanship](../../.agents/rules/code-quality.md): readable named phases, explicit trust-boundary types, no cryptic mixed-responsibility loops, comments for surprising invariants, focused Prettier/quality-lint on changed files. Escalate a major decomposition/architecture mismatch rather than growing a 1,000-line controller on autopilot.\n\n**Context compression continuity:** If context was compacted or a task resumes after a long gap, recover only the current Change/T-ID and its latest evidence before taking the next action. Recheck actual branch/HEAD, worktree changes, integration target, completed versus unverified checks, active resource ownership, and the next unfinished step. Do not trust a chat summary as execution proof, redo finished investigations without a changed premise, or create a parallel checkpoint system. Keep handoffs concise: scope, completed evidence, unresolved blocker, exact next action.

**Evidence:** report actual edits, tests/results, negative case, remaining blocker and spend. Never treat unrun checks as passed; no paid model calls or destructive resources without explicit approval. For repo-folder work consult [structure map](../../REPOSITORY-STRUCTURE.md).
